    208          //---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    209          /**
    210           * This method parses API020 feedbacks sent to a broadcast or exclusively to this node.
    211           * The function will ignore messages that do not satisfy the stringent Class B requirements:
    212           *      - The opcode of the message must match the opcode used by the Receive Channel
    213           *      - The sequence number must match the expected sequence number based on the previously received sequence number
    214           *      - The message must have originated from the expected source address for the Receive Channel
    215           *      - The source address in the message must match the expected source address for the Receive Channel
    216           *      - The destination address must match this node's bus address.
    217           *      - The safety data must be 0 to 11 bytes
    218           *      - The CRC at the end of the payload must be correct.
    219           * The function will only accept the data as valid if:
    220           *      - The last two messages were sequential (no lost message)
    221           *      - The time between the last two messages was less than the Receive Channel's timeout period.
    222           * @param fbk = Pointer to the received feedback message.
    223           */

